File system can be mounted by using MEMBLOCK driver mapped to the memory region
that contains ROMFS file system.

    const u32_t        romfs_address   = 0x08070000; // example address - use valid one
    const u32_t       *romfs_ptr       = cast(typeof(romfs_ptr), romfs_address);
    static const char *romfs_signature = "FPKG\n";

    if (memcmp(romfs_ptr, romfs_signature, strlen(romfs_signature)) == 0) {

            const u32_t romfs_size_offset_words = 16; // romfs header size
            u32_t       romfs_size = *(romfs_ptr + romfs_size_offset_words);

            if (romfs_size != UINT32_MAX) {
                    driver_init2("MEMBLOCK", 0, 0, "/dev/romfs",
                            &(MEMBLOCK_config_t) {
                                    .memory_address = romfs_address,
                                    .block_size     = romfs_size,
                                    .access         = O_RDONLY,
                            });

                    mount("romfs", "/dev/romfs", "/mnt", "validate");
            }
    }

POSIX simulator
---------------
The same image is used by the simulator (build/sim-romfs.bin), it is connected
as host disk 0 and mounted by the siminit program in the /etc folder:

    build/dnx-sim --disk 0=build/sim-romfs.bin:ro

Files:
    netmgr.conf  - network configuration used by the netmgr program when the
                   simulator is started with the --tap <name> option,
    dns.conf     - DNS servers (one address per line, max 128 bytes), used
                   when the host routes traffic of the TAP interface (NAT).
